---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { FileText, ArrowLeft } from 'lucide-react';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — ToolGenie"
  description="Read the ToolGenie Terms of Service governing the use of our free, client-side browser utilities."
  canonicalUrl="https://toolgenie.online/terms"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mb-8">
      <a 
        href="/" 
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-semibold hover:underline"
        style={{ color: 'var(--accent)' }}
      >
        <ArrowLeft size={14} />
        <span>Back to All Tools</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    {/* Header */}
    <div class="border-b pb-8 mb-10" style={{ borderColor: 'var(--border-subtle)' }}>
      <div 
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold mb-4 border"
        style={{
          backgroundColor: 'var(--bg-surface)',
          borderColor: 'var(--border-subtle)',
          color: 'var(--accent)'
        }}
      >
        <FileText size={14} />
        <span>Legal Agreement</span>
      </div>
      <h1 
        class="font-heading text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-4"
        style={{ color: 'var(--text-primary)' }}
      >
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm font-medium" style={{ color: 'var(--text-muted)' }}>
        Last updated: February 2026
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Content */}
    <div class="space-y-8 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed" style={{ color: 'var(--text-secondary)' }}>
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold tracking-tight" style={{ color: 'var(--text-primary)' }}>
          1. Agreement to Terms
        </h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using ToolGenie (toolgenie.online), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you disagree with any part of these terms, you may not use our utilities.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold tracking-tight" style={{ color: 'var(--text-primary)' }}>
          2. Description of Service
        </h2>
        <p>
          ToolGenie provides free, client-side browser utilities for file format conversion, compression, text processing, code formatting, and media manipulation. All processing is carried out entirely within the user&apos;s browser environment.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold tracking-tight" style={{ color: 'var(--text-primary)' }}>
          3. User Content &amp; Intellectual Property
        </h2>
        <p>
          You retain 100% of all rights, title, and interest (including copyright) in any files, text, images, or documents you process through ToolGenie. Because files are processed in-memory in your browser, ToolGenie never claims, receives, or holds any license or ownership over your content.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold tracking-tight" style={{ color: 'var(--text-primary)' }}>
          4. Disclaimer of Warranties
        </h2>
        <p>
          ToolGenie is provided on an &ldquo;AS IS&rdquo; and &ldquo;AS AVAILABLE&rdquo; basis without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied. While we strive for absolute mathematical precision and high-fidelity output across all tools, you agree that you are solely responsible for verifying critical output files.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-heading text-xl font-bold tracking-tight" style={{ color: 'var(--text-primary)' }}>
          5. Contact Information
        </h2>
        <p>
          For legal or terms inquiries, please email:
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:farhanaly.io3@gmail.com" class="font-bold hover:underline" style={{ color: 'var(--accent)' }}>
            farhanaly.io3@gmail.com
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
